# `id`, `file`, `old` (must occur EXACTLY once), `new`, optional `equivalent` and `targets`. NOT RUN YET (written edit-only on wip/tb3,
# 2026-11-10, nothing compiled or run): every KILL below is read off the rows of wip/tb3 325d4ede; the first hand-run replaces this header
# with the true verdicts.
# THE ROWS (TA = test/core_lang/test_tabling_answers_swipl.jl, ONE program consulted by swipl and the kernel, rows run IN ORDER in one database,
# answers pinned from swipl 10.1.20): taq01-taq13 = `$tbl_answer`/3, `$tbl_answer_c`/4, `$tbl_wkl_add_answer`/4 registered, errors, an empty trie
# (+ the white-box @tests of the registration table in the taq testset); taa01-taa11 = `$tbl_answer`/3 of completed tables of `ta_p/1`, `ta_pair/2`
# (taa01 is the FIRST call of the variant `ta_p(_)`, taa06-taa11 call it again: the complete-table fast path, S_TABLED and `tbl_complete_answer_clause`);
# tas01-tas23 = answer subsumption (max, min, first, last, lattice(ta_join/3), po(ta_lt/2), two moded args; the moded variant is `$ta_max$1(_)`;
# tas15-tas17 the first calls of `ta_max(a|b|c, X)`, tas18 a bound moded argument (uninstantiation_error), tas21-tas23 the status and the answers
# of the moded trie). The taa and tas rows RUN ONCE TB2 AND TB5 ARE STACKED (start_tabling, completion); taq needs TB3 + TB2's get_worklist.
# THE FOUR CLASSES (every mutant id says which; DEFERRED and SURVIVES-UNTIL-ROW live in the list `DEFERRED` at the end, not in MUTANTS):
#   KILL <row>        the row's @test fails (the row's name is the rowid of TA's `_TA_CASES`, or the testset of a white-box @test);
#   EQUIVALENT        `equivalent:` carries the reason with a file:line (the driver does not run it as a kill target);
#   DEFERRED KILL <owner step>: the mutated code is NOT reached by any TA row; the OWNER must add the row named (the program has to be recursive
#       or to carry delays, TB5/TB4; a ground table called twice and a trie property, TB5/TR2): the survivor of the first battery is
#       EXPECTED and is not a defect of the port; listed in `DEFERRED` below with its owner;
#   SURVIVES-UNTIL-ROW (owner TB3): a TB3 row is still to be added to TA.
# WHY THE FAST PATH IS NOT ROW-VISIBLE (read off the code, wip/tb3): when the complete-table fast path (S_TABLED -> tbl_complete_answer_clause) is
# NOT taken, S_CALLWRAPPER calls start_tabling/3, which answers a complete table from the same trie: the answers are the same. A mutant that only
# SKIPS the fast path (a wrong condition, a wrong lookup) therefore survives every answer row; its only witness is the counter
# `atrie.gen_call` (`call_complete_table`, pl-tabling.jl:1039), read in swipl by `trie_property(T, gen_call_count(N))` (pl-trie.c:2648-2703; the
# kernel's `$trie_property` has no such property at wip/tb3: grep gen_call_count in src/ is empty). Owner of the witness row: TB5 (the row), TR2 (the
# property). A mutant that CORRUPTS what the fast path hands on (the skeleton, the frame slots, ARGP) is killed by taa06-taa11.
# The same holds for the RETURN value of `tbl_add_answer`/`wkl_mode_add_answer`: `$tbl_wkl_add_answer`/4 only succeeds or fails, and `delim/4`
# (boot/tabling.pl:695-696) fails after both: a mutant of the return value alone is EQUIVALENT; a mutant of an EFFECT on the trie is a kill.
# TARGETS (audit D-0238): TA (the step's file); TM = test_tabling_min_swipl.jl (T3: consults tabled programs, runs the S_TABLED supervisor, `$tbl_trienode`);
# for the registration table and trie_gen's data kind also TR = test_trie_swipl.jl and TP = test_trie_preds_swipl.jl (trie_gen/trie_gen_raw, the
# callers of `unify_delay_info`). NOT listed: test_tabling_state_swipl.jl (the table state of TB0: reads `ld.tabling`, none of this code),
# test_static_analysis.jl (the CI's static job, not a mutation target).
